  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Illi nam duplici confuta palliaP-</l>
    <l n="2">anno, &amp; crassa domum penula protegit.</l>
    <l n="3">Illi perpetuis ignibus atria-</l>
    <l n="4">Propellunt hyemes lucida frigidas.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Illi puniceo purpura murice-</l>
    <l n="6">Ardet tincta:micat Sestibus illitum-</l>
    <l n="7">Aurum coccineis, atque tapetibus-</l>
    <l n="8">Claros nobilibus condecorat thoros.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Illi interproceres conspicuos sedet-</l>
    <l n="10">Coniux purpurea splendidor toga:</l>
    <l n="11">Quum lites remouent Abramidum, &amp; simul-</l>
    <l n="12">Portis turba frequens conuenit Srbium.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Quantas perpetuis cogit opes lucris,</l>
    <l n="14">Quum telas Tyriis syndonibus pares,</l>
    <l n="15">Et quae pinxit acu mollia nobili-</l>
    <l n="16">Diuendit pretiis carbasa grandibus.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Hinc mentem trepidis intrepidam gerit-</l>
    <l n="18">Rebus:non dubij temporis exitum,</l>
    <l n="19">Casusve ancipites, aut pauet anxia-</l>
    <l n="20">Quae Sventura dies durior apparat.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Illi Serba fluunt pectore candido-</l>
    <l n="22">Sempermellifluis picta leporibus:</l>
    <l n="23">Et puram loquitur quae sapientiam-</l>
    <l n="24">Spirent, quaeque nitens gratia temperet.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Ædes mane suas sollicitis Sigil-</l>
    <l n="26">Lustrat luminibus, singula dispicit,</l>
    <l n="27">Vt se quisque gerat, sordibus &amp; procul</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse page; the text is set in italic. Some words are doubtful: "tincta", "Srbium", "Sventura" and "Sestibus" are read with uncertainty, and the initial letters of some lines appear to be swash capitals. The line-end at "Sigil" and "procul" may run on. No catchword or signature visible.</notes>
